**`go/ast/inspector/inspector.go`** — Added `Len()` method after `New()`:

```go
// Len returns the number of AST nodes in the files supplied to [New],
// the same count that [ast.Inspect] visits.
func (in *Inspector) Len() int {
	n := 0
	for i := range in.events {
		if in.events[i].index > int32(i) {
			n++
		}
	}
	return n
}
```

The method counts push events by checking `ev.index > int32(i)`, which is the same predicate used in `Preorder`, `Nodes`, and `WithStack` to identify push events (those whose `index` field points forward to a matching pop).

**`go/ast/inspector/inspector_test.go`** — Added `TestInspectLen` which independently counts nodes via `ast.Inspect` and compares against `inspect.Len()`.

